---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import CadenceTimeline from '../../components/CadenceTimeline.astro';
---
<Layout
  title="Website rebuild that lifts conversion | Kadanco"
  description="A site and story that match the company you are now, plus an instrumented funnel you can keep improving. Repositioning, brand and website rebuild, sales collateral, CRO and lifecycle, run by two operators."
>
  <main id="top">

    <!-- ===================== HERO ===================== -->
    <section class="hero" data-theme="dark">
      <div class="container">
        <span class="eyebrow">Use case &middot; Conversion rebuild</span>
        <h1>Your site describes the company<br><span class="hl">you used to be.</span></h1>
        <p class="lead">You moved upmarket, changed what you sell, or learned who actually buys. The website did not follow. We reposition around where you are now, rebuild the site to match, and instrument the funnel so conversion keeps improving after launch.</p>
        <div class="hero-cta">
          <button class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" data-open-modal>Get a free audit</button>
          <p class="hero-cta-note">We'll show you where the funnel leaks, then we fix it.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ===================== THE GAP ===================== -->
    <section class="section band-paper" data-theme="light">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="split">
          <div class="content">
            <span class="eyebrow dark">The gap</span>
            <h2>The traffic is fine. <span class="hl-indigo">The argument is not.</span></h2>
          </div>
          <div class="content">
            <p class="lead">Most conversion problems are not design problems. The page is loading, people are arriving, and the words on it are still selling the previous version of the business. A redesign that only changes how the site looks moves nothing, because the leak was never visual. It was the argument, and the fact that nobody was measuring where visitors quietly gave up.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ===================== WHERE IT LEAKS (funnel) ===================== -->
    <section class="section" data-theme="light">
      <div class="container">
        <span class="eyebrow indigo">Where it leaks</span>
        <h2>Four places you lose them, <span class="hl-indigo">before sales ever sees them.</span></h2>
        <div style="max-width:1000px;margin:44px auto 0">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 1120 380" data-anim="diagram" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" style="width:100%;height:auto;display:block" role="img" aria-label="A funnel narrowing through four stages: traffic arrives, the page makes its case, the form gets filled, and sales gets a real lead. The first three stages leak because the message does not match the ad, the positioning describes the old company, and nothing follows up fast enough.">
            <rect x="60" y="20" width="680" height="64" rx="12" fill="#3B38DF"/>
            <text x="84" y="60" font-family="Fira Sans" font-size="18" font-weight="600" fill="#FFFFFF">Traffic arrives</text>

            <rect x="60" y="102" width="560" height="64" rx="12" fill="#3B38DF" opacity="0.8"/>
            <text x="84" y="142" font-family="Fira Sans" font-size="18" font-weight="600" fill="#FFFFFF">The page makes its case</text>

            <rect x="60" y="184" width="440" height="64" rx="12" fill="#3B38DF" opacity="0.58"/>
            <text x="84" y="224" font-family="Fira Sans" font-size="18" font-weight="600" fill="#FFFFFF">The form gets filled</text>

            <rect x="60" y="266" width="320" height="64" rx="12" fill="#DAFF02"/>
            <text x="84" y="306" font-family="Fira Sans" font-size="18" font-weight="700" fill="#201E1F">A real lead</text>

            <g stroke="#B2B1FF" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="6 6">
              <path d="M748 52 L 778 52"/>
              <path d="M628 134 L 778 134"/>
              <path d="M508 216 L 778 216"/>
            </g>
            <g font-family="Fira Sans" font-size="15" font-weight="500" fill="#5A5A72">
              <text x="790" y="57">The message does not match the ad</text>
              <text x="790" y="139">Positioning describes the old company</text>
              <text x="790" y="221">Nothing follows up fast enough</text>
            </g>
            <text x="790" y="303" font-family="Fira Sans" font-size="15" font-weight="600" fill="#3B38DF">What you actually wanted</text>
          </svg>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ===================== WHAT WE REBUILD ===================== -->
    <section class="section band-deep" data-theme="dark">
      <div class="container">
        <span class="eyebrow peri">What we rebuild</span>
        <h2>The argument first, <span class="hl">then the site.</span></h2>
        <div class="grid cols-3" style="margin-top:48px;text-align:left">
          <div class="card">
            <h3>Repositioning</h3>
            <p>We reposition around the company you are now: who buys, what they compare you to, and why you win when you win.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="card">
            <h3>Brand and website</h3>
            <p>A rebuild that carries the new argument, page by page, instead of a redesign that only changes the surface.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="card">
            <h3>Sales collateral</h3>
            <p>The deck, the one-pagers and the follow-up material saying the same thing as the site, so the story survives the handoff.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="card">
            <h3>Conversion optimisation</h3>
            <p>Forms, calls to action and page structure worked on continuously, with the funnel instrumented so you can see what moved.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="card">
            <h3>Lifecycle and automation</h3>
            <p>What happens after the form: routing, follow-up and nurture that runs on time instead of when someone remembers.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ===================== WHAT YOU OWN ===================== -->
    <section class="section band-paper" data-theme="light">
      <div class="container">
        <span class="eyebrow dark">What you own</span>
        <h2>A site that matches you, <span class="hl-indigo">and keeps getting better.</span></h2>
        <div class="grid cols-3" style="margin-top:48px;text-align:left">
          <div class="card">
            <h3>A current story</h3>
            <p>Positioning and a site that describe the company today, so sales stops apologising for the website on calls.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="card">
            <h3>An instrumented funnel</h3>
            <p>Every step measured, so the next improvement is a decision from data instead of an opinion in a meeting.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="card">
            <h3>Something you can keep</h3>
            <p>A site your team can run and extend, not a bespoke build that needs the agency back for every change.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ===================== FIRST 90 DAYS ===================== -->
    <section class="section band-deep" data-theme="dark">
      <div class="container">
        <span class="eyebrow peri">The first 90 days</span>
        <h2>Fix the argument, <span class="hl">then ship.</span></h2>
        <CadenceTimeline
          steps={[
            { n: "01", title: "Map", body: "We audit the funnel with real numbers, interview customers and sales, and agree the positioning the site should be making." },
            { n: "02", title: "Build", body: "We rebuild the pages that carry the argument first, with tracking in place from day one, not added afterwards." },
            { n: "03", title: "Ship", amp: "& iterate", body: "Live in weeks, then improved continuously against what the funnel actually shows.", loop: "and conversion climbs" },
          ]}
        />
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ===================== ONE USE CASE NOTE ===================== -->
    <section class="section center" data-theme="light">
      <div class="container">
        <p class="lead" style="max-width:720px;margin:0 auto">
          A conversion rebuild is one of the ways teams put Kadanco to work. It is one of several. The same two operators plan and run product, marketing and sales for B2B companies. <a class="hl-indigo" href="/">See everything we do →</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ===================== FINAL CTA ===================== -->
    <section class="section cta-band center" data-theme="dark">
      <div class="container">
        <span class="eyebrow peri">Lets Talk</span>
        <h2>Ready to fix <span class="hl">the funnel?</span></h2>
        <p class="lead" style="margin-top:20px">Tell us where you think you're losing people. We'll show you where it actually happens, then we'll fix it.</p>
        <div class="cta-actions">
          <button class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" data-open-modal>Get a free audit</button>
        </div>
        <p class="cta-note">Free, no obligation. We'll get back to you quickly.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

  </main>
</Layout>
